  message: "Staleness audit 2026-07-21: the named root-cause hypothesis is falsified. additional_file_centrality_scores is computed by compute_symbol_mention_centrality_batch (cli.py:9829-9843) — a ripgrep/regex symbol-mention DENSITY scan (max_file_size=100KB) over NON-source config/doc candidate files only (content_source_paths at cli.py:9817-9818 excludes all source symbols), invoking NO embedding model; only readme_description uses embeddings, on a single README. It does not touch the 14.6k Java files. The 60min timeout headline itself is UNVERIFIED (>60min repro out of scope). Retitled to drop the embedding hypothesis; the real bottleneck over >1M LOC / 193k Import edges (analysis/linker/finalize) needs a fresh profile."  # c9be
- op: discuss  # ba10
  at: '2026-08-17T21:05:15Z'  # ba10
  by: agent  # ba10
  actor: jgstern_agent  # ba10
  clock: 6  # ba10
  nonce: ba10  # ba10
  message: "REFRAMED BY THE 2026-08-17 PERF CLOSE, and deliberately NOT parked with the rest.\n\nThis item used to carry two jobs: (a) the \"tens of minutes\" cell that would ungate\nWI-madut/WI-zagij, and (b) an unexplained >60min run. Job (a) is gone — those\nitems are parked wont_do+someday. Job (b) stands on its own and is the reason this\nstays open: a ~14.6k-file repo taking >60 minutes with the bottleneck UNLOCATED is\na possible PATHOLOGY, and the perf close was about declining to chase diminishing\nreturns, not about tolerating an unexplained order-of-magnitude outlier.\n\nWHAT CHANGED IN ITS FAVOUR: the instrument that would locate it now exists.\nscripts/measure-survey-phase-split.py attributes wall clock to phase functions\nwith inclusive/exclusive accounting and prints the residual as UNATTRIBUTED, so\nthis no longer requires a bespoke investigation. Note it is a Java repo, so the\ntree-sitter locate path dominates — the one path this monorepo could not exercise\n(#394's quadratic was in the hand-written python locator; tree-sitter descends\nnatively via descendant_for_byte_range).\n\nIf the split shows an ordinary profile, this closes as \"big repo is big\" and the\nperf posture is unchanged. If it shows another single-function anomaly like\n#394's, that is a new measured pathology and the re-open trigger the close names."  # ba10
